    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: buffons-needle-oq-02\n\nInsights accumulated during research on this problem.\n\n---\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nThe problem concerns the 3D Buffon formula for a polygonal curve of total length L dropped on parallel planes with spacing d. The expected crossing count is stated as L/(2d). The key constant is the sphere average E_{S^2}[|cos phi|] = 1/2, computed from the integral of sin theta |cos theta| over [0, pi]. The local statement also compares this 3D factor with the 2D Buffon factor 2/pi.\n\n---\n\n## Insights\n\n- The stated 3D crossing factor is alpha_3 = 1/2.\n- The integral calculation splits |cos theta| at pi/2, using cos theta on [0, pi/2] and -cos theta on [pi/2, pi].\n- The comparison goal is alpha_3 = 1/2 < 2/pi = alpha_2.\n\n---\n\n## Dead Ends\n\nNo dead ends are documented in the local research notes.\n"
